---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<Base title="About" description="About Thierry Heumann, a QA and test automation lead who builds small, focused web apps.">
  <article class="pt-10 pb-8">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">About</h1>

    <div class="prose mt-8">
      <p>
        I'm Thierry Heumann. "The Apps" (or "TH e-apps") is where the things I build end up.
      </p>

      <p>
        I've spent over a decade as a QA lead and test automation engineer, building
        quality strategy and automation frameworks for SaaS companies. I got good
        at finding the missing parts of software before users did, and at working
        closely enough with product and engineering teams to help prevent them in
        the first place. Watching where software leaves people stranded is a
        decent education in what to build instead.
      </p>

      <p>
        Recently, alongside my QA career, I started building my own things. Most of them come from the
        same place: a group of people trying to coordinate something, and a group
        chat that isn't up to the job. Chat is great for banter and bad for state.
        Who's actually coming? Who paid? Is there room for one more? The answer is
        buried in a thread nobody wants to scroll.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="/work/whosin">whosin</a> and <a href="/work/fphelp">FPheLp</a> do
        exactly that, in different contexts. They aren't replacing chat. They take
        the handful of things chat does badly (RSVPs, payments, standings, results)
        and stay out of the way for everything else.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Feedback, questions, or an idea for an app or website you'd like built.
        Please reach out.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm also open to QA engineering and test automation roles.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/thierryheumann/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >
          LinkedIn
        </a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> | </span>
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
